                <h2>Why Balance Alerts Are Critical for Ad Performance</h2>
<p>In overseas advertising, running out of account balance often causes more damage than expected—algorithms need to relearn, bidding advantages are lost, and the prime window for high-performing creatives closes prematurely.</p>
<p>Many teams assume "as long as there's money in the account, nothing will go wrong," but reality shows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Time zone gaps</strong>: China-US time differences cause payment approval delays, leaving midnight balance emergencies unattended</li>
<li><strong>Payment limits</strong>: Credit card daily limits, monthly billing date freezes</li>
<li><strong>Review triggers</strong>: Large deposits trigger platform risk controls, causing temporary account restrictions</li>
</ul>
<p>This article provides an actionable checklist for complete balance protection.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Part 1: Alert Configuration Steps</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Establish Alert Threshold Baseline</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Daily Spend Level</th>
<th>Recommended Alert Threshold</th>
<th>Recommended Safe Balance</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Daily spend &lt; $500</td>
<td>1.5x daily spend</td>
<td>3x daily spend</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Daily spend $500-2000</td>
<td>2x daily spend</td>
<td>4x daily spend</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Daily spend &gt; $2000</td>
<td>2.5x daily spend</td>
<td>5x daily spend</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>: □ Calculated 30-day average daily spend for each account □ Recorded thresholds in operations documentation □ Notified finance team</p>
<h3>Step 2: Configure Native Platform Alerts</h3>
<p><strong>Meta Business Manager</strong>: Settings → Payments → Payment methods → Budget alerts → Set amount threshold → Add notification email</p>
<p><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Tools &amp; Settings → Billing → Alerts → Create alert → Select trigger → Bind email and SMS</p>
<p><strong>TikTok Ads</strong>: Assets → Billing → Budget alerts → Enable → Set threshold and notification method</p>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>: □ Completed alert setup on all three platforms □ Alerts sent to both operations and finance □ SMS notifications enabled (to prevent email delays)</p>
<h3>Step 3: Establish External Monitoring</h3>
<p>Platform alerts may have delays or miss notifications, so add external monitoring:</p>
<ul>
<li>Track all account balances in Excel/Feishu, update in morning meetings</li>
<li>Maintain deposit records with estimated depletion times</li>
<li>Enable balance monitoring notifications on multi-account management tools</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist</strong>: □ Created account balance tracking sheet □ Daily operations staff responsible for updates □ Finance CC rule established</p>
<hr />
<h2>Part 2: Emergency Response Checklist for Deposit Interruptions</h2>
<p>When receiving balance alerts or discovering insufficient funds, respond quickly:</p>
<h3>☑ Immediate Actions (within 5 minutes)</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Confirm the alerted account's daily budget and spend velocity</li>
<li>[ ] Estimate remaining balance depletion time</li>
<li>[ ] Check if delivery has auto-paused</li>
<li>[ ] Screenshot account balance as record</li>
</ul>
<h3>☑ Initiate Deposit (within 10 minutes)</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Log into preferred deposit channel (credit card/bank transfer/payment platform)</li>
<li>[ ] Verify deposit amount: no less than 3x daily spend</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm deposit arrival time (credit card usually instant, bank transfer 1-4 hours)</li>
<li>[ ] Switch to backup method if primary channel fails</li>
</ul>
<h3>☑ Notify Stakeholders</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Inform performance marketers account is recharged, monitor recovery status</li>
<li>[ ] Contact platform support for expedited processing if issues persist</li>
<li>[ ] Log this alert event for post-mortem review</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Part 3: Preventive Preparation Checklist</h2>
<h3>Payment Channel Backup</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Primary: Corporate credit card (with appropriate limit)</li>
<li>[ ] Backup 1: Corporate bank transfer (account info confirmed in advance)</li>
<li>[ ] Backup 2: Third-party payment platform (e.g., Yiyu payment service)</li>
<li>[ ] Ensure all channels verified and have no failure history</li>
</ul>
<h3>Financial Reserve Plan</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Estimate next month's spend budget for each account at month start</li>
<li>[ ] Pre-approve large deposit requests with finance to avoid month-end credit limits</li>
<li>[ ] Maintain dedicated ad account reserve fund with 3-5 days' spend liquidity</li>
</ul>
<h3>Peak Period Contingency</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Recharge to safe levels 3 days before major sales events</li>
<li>[ ] Set higher alert thresholds (1.5x normal)</li>
<li>[ ] Schedule on-call coverage during peak periods, check balance every 4 hours</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: What if balance doesn't update immediately after deposit?</strong><br />
A: Credit card deposits usually arrive within 5 minutes; bank transfers may take 1-4 hours. If beyond expected time, first verify payment receipt is uploaded correctly, then contact platform support with payment reference number to expedite.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Which account should I prioritize if multiple accounts are alerting?</strong><br />
A: Sort by daily spend—prioritize the account with highest consumption. If spend is equal, prioritize restoring the best-performing account or the one with trending creatives.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to handle when platform temporarily restricts deposits?</strong><br />
A: This is a common risk control response, usually automatically lifted within 24 hours. Switch to backup payment channels or contact platform support to explain the situation and request restriction removal.</p>
